## Why This Is Asked
This question tests deep production debugging skills, including multi-tenant cache management, Redis eviction policies, and safe rollout procedures under traffic.

## Key Concepts
- Redis eviction policies (volatile-lru, allkeys-lru, etc.) and TTL management
- Multi-tenant namespace isolation in Redis using key prefixes
- Canary rollout strategies (e.g., Argo Rollouts or manual phased deployments)
- Observability: Redis INFO metrics, hit/miss ratios, and application latency metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Verify current eviction policy
const evictionPolicy = await redis.configGet('maxmemory-policy');
console.log('Current eviction policy:', evictionPolicy);

// Check keyspace stats
const info = await redis.info('stats');
const hits = info.match(/keyspace_hits:(\d+)/)[1];
const misses = info.match(/keyspace_misses:(\d+)/)[1];
const hitRate = hits / (hits + misses);
console.log('Hit rate:', hitRate);
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical data quality controls, schema evolution discipline, and safe deployment practices in multi-tenant streaming environments.

## Key Concepts
- Schema Registry with AVRO and compatibility enforcement
- Per-tenant schema namespaces and semantic versioning
- Real-time drift detection in Flink processing pipeline
- Automated quarantine and alerting mechanisms
- Circuit breaker patterns for data quality protection

## Code Example
```java
// Flink schema validation with drift detection
public class SchemaValidator extends ProcessFunction<GenericRecord, GenericRecord> {
    private final SchemaRegistryClient registry;

    @Override
    public void processElement(GenericRecord record, Context ctx) {
        try {
            Schema schema = registry.getLatestSchema(tenantTopic);
            if (!isValidAgainstSchema(record, schema)) {
                ctx.output(quarantineTag, record);
                alertDashboard("SCHEMA_DRIFT", tenantTopic);
            } else {
                ctx.output(validTag, record);
            }
        } catch (Exception e) {
            ctx.output(errorTag, record);
        }
    }
}
```

